&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Game Designer &lt;/strong&gt;(Level Design) on the Unpublished R&amp;amp;D Product team, you will partner with designers, artists, and engineers to create, iterate, and improve player-focused level design experiences. You will contribute hands-on to building, tuning, and refining gameplay spaces while collaborating across disciplines to solve design challenges through rapid iteration and playtesting. You will thrive in an evolving development environment where experimentation, collaboration, and continuous improvement are essential to delivering high-quality player experiences. You will report into the Director, Game Design of the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly implement and iterate on gameplay spaces and environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and improve gameplay spaces that deliver engaging player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and promote best practices for future level design work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop multiple design solutions while clearly communicating trade-offs and implementation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize rapid prototyping and playtesting to validate design solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear design documentation that can be understood and implemented across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with designers, artists, engineers, and other partners to deliver cohesive player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate feedback and continuously iterate toward high-quality design outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional experience in Level Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated excellence in Level Design through shipped titles or equivalent professional work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency building levels using an established game engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using environments to guide player progression, support gameplay systems, improve navigation, and enhance player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of player-centered level design principles and iterative development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in Mandarin Chinese.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading Level Design efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a live game or live service product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with prototyping and iterative game development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant proficiency (3+ years) using Unreal Engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;l

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to critical and player acclaim. As the most played video game in the world, over 100 million play every month. Players form the foundation of our community and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Game Designer on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends: Wild Rift&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own and evolve the map layouts, terrain architecture, neutral objectives, and jungle monster systems that drive the strategic depth and pacing of Summoner’s Rift. You will design, implement, and optimize core map features, ensuring they deliver an engaging, fair, and dynamically competitive environment optimized for a mobile audience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with Balance and System designers to integrate structural map changes and objective reworks into the core SR gameplay. You will utilize your spatial design expertise and player empathy to navigate complex design challenges, ensuring every environmental and objective adjustment aligns with Riot&#39;s design philosophy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the lifecycle, structural map design, and live iteration of core map features, neutral objectives, and jungle monster mechanics on Summoner&#39;s Rift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set quality and execution standards for terrain layout, map visibility, and objective mechanics, delivering high-clarity documentation that enables seamless cross-functional implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Balance Designer and System Designer to ensure all map terrain changes, objective overhauls, or monster system adaptations safeguard competitive integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize player feedback, high-level telemetry, and game data to diagnose systemic flaws or communication bottlenecks, driving long-term map and environmental updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in professional Game Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in either Map Design or Level Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can create complex mechanics and systems with attention to the player impacts and downstream effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep level of understanding, passion, and engagement with MOBA games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a live product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is familiar with the LoL IP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise, a collaborative spirit, and decision-making that prioritizes the delight of players. We will be looking at your past studies, experience, and your personal relationship with games.

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is seeking a Senior Game Designer to join our Stumble Guys team!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Stumble Guys is one of our most recent hits, with millions of fans joining the party every single day, constantly keeping it at the top of the charts in over 50 countries and with the ambition of becoming nothing less than a beloved franchise and to be played for many years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;This is a key role within the Gameplay cluster. As a Senior Gameplay Designer, you’ll help shape the core player experience by designing abilities, mechanics, and gameplay systems that are fun, readable, scalable, and replayable. You’ll work closely with multidisciplinary teams to create gameplay that reaches millions of players around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate has a strong understanding of gameplay design, player psychology, and multiplayer games. They are an excellent communicator, comfortable collaborating across disciplines, and able to turn ideas into clear, actionable designs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design new gameplay mechanics, abilities, and interactive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create engaging gameplay experiences that work across different maps, game modes, and player skill levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear design documentation, specifications, and implementation briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Engineering, Art, UX/UI, Production, Product Analytics, QA, and other designers to bring features from concept to release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype, iterate, and refine gameplay features using player feedback, playtests, and live data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain gameplay quality, balance, readability, and consistency across the game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute ideas that improve the overall player experience and support the long-term evolution of Stumble Guys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with designers, engineers, artists, production, audio, QA, community, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the data team to build enduring processes for analyzing, assessing, and balancing various gameplay elements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong gameplay design skills with a solid understanding of multiplayer gameplay and player interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to gather feedback, align stakeholders, and iterate collaboratively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for playing and analyzing games across multiple genres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently while thriving in a highly collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing clear technical design documentation, including design briefs, feature specifications, and implementation documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with the ability to use playtest results and data to improve designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in combat design, level design or narrative design are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
